    "resolvable": true,
    "resolved": true,
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3918195019,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "[P1] A refused shot records PvP grace. `vessel_fire_permitted()` calls `vessel_pvp_permitted(ch, target)` first; that helper writes and persists grace on the target and the gunner hull when the gunner and target owner consent. If the gunner is a permit holder but the firing hull owner has PVP off, the later owner check rejects the shot, yet the target owner can still attack the gunner hull after its owner logs out. When the owner does consent, the second `vessel_pvp_permitted(owner, target)` call overwrites the target grace attacker with the owner, so the permit holder who fired loses grace if the target owner logs out. Make both consent checks side-effect free, then record one engagement for the actual gunner only after all firing checks pass. Add assertions for unchanged grace on refusal and the actual gunner name on approval.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
        },
