      {
        "id": 3919039419,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Fixed in 9b8c3eb02. 9112a7293 adds the explicit `!= 0` that clang-tidy wanted on the `str_cmp()`.\n\n- Both consent checks now use a side-effect-free `vessel_pvp_consented()`. `vessel_fire_permitted()` records one engagement, for the actual gunner, only after both consents pass.\n- `shipfire` now checks consent after the range and arc gates, so a shot that never fires records nothing.\n- A second effect showed up while tracing the fix. Once grace names the permit holder, the old owner check (grace keyed to the owner's name) would refuse every shot after the target's owner logged out, so nobody could keep firing. With the target's owner offline, `vessel_hull_owner_consents()` now needs only the hull owner's PvP flag. The gunner's own grace has already been checked.\n\n`Test_vessel_fire_records_grace_for_the_gunner_only` checks four things:\n\n- A refused shot leaves grace unchanged on both hulls.\n- An approved shot records the gunner's name.\n- After the target's owner logs out, the gunner may continue and the hull owner may not.\n- The gunner is stopped once the hull owner turns PvP off.\n\nOn the previous code it fails with `expected <> but was <Mira>`.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
