      {
        "id": 3918196061,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "[P2] The custom departure level fails open when its database lookup fails. `vessel_ship_min_level()` returns the class minimum when `vessel_prototype_ensure_schema()` fails, and lines 137-145 do the same after a failed SELECT. For a raft prototype configured with `min_level = 30`, a level-1 captain can issue `setsail`, `autopilot on`, `assignpilot`, or `setschedule` during a transient database failure because the required level becomes 1. The new test even asserts this fallback with `mysql_available = FALSE`, but never covers a higher prototype override in that state. Keep the effective level on the live hull or refuse the departure when an existing prototype override cannot be read; do not substitute a lower class level for an unknown configured requirement.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
