      {
        "id": 3919039578,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Fixed in 45d378d92.\n\n- When a prototype-backed hull's level cannot be read (database unavailable or a failed SELECT), `vessel_ship_min_level()` returns `VESSEL_MIN_LEVEL_UNKNOWN`.\n- `vessel_helm_level_refused()` then refuses mortals with a harbor-records message. Staff and NPC pilots are still exempt.\n- A prototype row that no longer exists still means the class minimum, since there is no override to honor.\n- The `mysql_available = FALSE` test now expects a prototype-backed hull to be refused, even for a level-22 captain on a warship.\n- The DB-backed test drops `min_level` from its fixture table to force a failed SELECT on the level-28 prototype, and asserts the refusal.\n\nOn the previous code it fails with `expected <-1> but was <1>`.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
