      {
        "id": 3919039963,
        "type": "DiffNote",
        "body": "Fixed in 45d378d92.\n\n- `vessel_prototype_ensure_schema()` (CREATE plus ALTER) now runs only at boot, from `boot_db()`.\n- `vessel_ship_min_level()`, `shipbrowse`, `shipbuy`, and `vedit` all ran the same new ALTER on every command. They now only check `mysql_available && conn != NULL` and read.\n- The DB-backed test drops the `min_level` column, calls the departure check, and asserts the column is still missing. The old `ADD COLUMN IF NOT EXISTS` would have restored it.",
