  {
    "id": "09c128c9449344e39375f1c72dbba45236048a8b",
    "individual_note": true,
    "resolvable": false,
    "notes": [
      {
        "id": 3919040746,
        "type": null,
        "body": "## Review round addressed\n\nAll five findings are fixed, with a reply on each thread. The branch was 0 commits behind `master`, so no rebase was needed.\n\n| Finding | Fix |\n| -- | -- |\n| P1 refused shot records PvP grace | 9b8c3eb02, 9112a7293 |\n| P1 DDL on the departure path | 45d378d92 |\n| P2 hull level fails open | 45d378d92 |\n| P2 gate cleanup deletes other prototypes | 5ce14ee75 |\n| P3 temporary path in the validation record | 7e2ad8333 |\n\nThe first local CI run also failed two jobs on the original S1 commits, so I fixed those too:\n\n- `integration-database-migration`: `vessels_phase18_schema.sql` failed on a fresh `master_schema.sql`, which has no `ship_prototypes`, `vessel_bounties`, or `wages_owed`. The schema now creates them the way the server's boot DDL does (0f05741bc). It applies cleanly to a fresh schema and to one that already has Phases 02/04/06/07, twice, and again after rollback.\n- `test-coverage`: the new `vessel_owner_cap` config parse was executed by no test. `Test_vessel_owner_cap_config_is_clamped` now covers it (26bd5f995).\n\n### Verification\n\n- `make test-all` passed with DB cases on an isolated MariaDB: 1869 CuTest cases plus the protocol harness. The later commits add one test; the vessel filter (98 tests) passes on 26bd5f995.\n- All six live vessel gates passed on `5ce14ee7` (installed SHA-256 `d5109a1e...`): tactical, events, boarding, lookout, narrative, and rules. They ran in a private namespace against a copy of the development DB. The rules run reported prototype 30 and removed only that one.\n- New and changed tests fail on the pre-fix code:\n  - `expected <> but was <Mira>` for the grace fix\n  - `expected <-1> but was <1>` for the level fix\n- Local CI matrix (`scripts/ci/local/run.py`, all jobs) on 26bd5f995: all 33 jobs pass, including 1870 CuTest cases with DB in the unit, sanitizer, memory-check, and coverage jobs, and the clang-tidy baseline.\n\n**Merge:** use the project's merge commit without squashing. The commits are split one defect per commit, and the validation record cites `5ce14ee7`.",
        "author": {
          "id": 42759441,
          "username": "max757",
          "public_email": "",
          "name": "Max aka Mosheh",
          "state": "active",
          "locked": false,
          "avatar_url": "https://secure.gravatar.com/avatar/3c7c169343bd7d0f4575137ce8065aee7cb44024d447bbfe66d773133a81c43e?s=80&d=identicon",
          "web_url": "https://gitlab.com/max757"
        },
